keywords:
  - flask
  - information retrieval
  - bm25
  - reproducible research
  - web application architecture
abstract: >-
  FlaskVerseHub is a knowledge-management web application that serves as a
  reference implementation for Flask: typed SQLAlchemy models, REST and
  GraphQL interfaces over a shared service layer, real-time events,
  observability, and an information-retrieval engine (BM25, BM25+, TF-IDF)
  evaluated on a seeded synthetic benchmark with bootstrap confidence
  intervals that continuous integration reproduces exactly.
